A||||9||Shaun41178||glowing manifolds at any time?||||5||
Z||000000||Shaun41178||01-27-2001||08:15 PM||||Are the exhaust manifolds supposed to glow at any time?  I was out in the dark and after 3-4 minutes afer i started my car the manifolds started glowing.  i would rev it up to about 2k on the tach and they would get even more red.  i am doubting this is normal but I thought since it being nighttime it would be more visible to see them glow.<P>I must tell you all that i have my egr tube blocked off at the intake manifold.  i checked the gasket and it did not have any visible holes so i reinstalled it and put rtv around it as well just for good insurance.  My egr pipe is still connected to the egr valve itself but the tube is broken and just vents to my engine compartment.  Could the engine be sucking air somehow through that egr tube through the valve and then through the small vacuum line that goes to the egr valve?  Are there any other places that are prone to developing vacumum leaks like any lines in particular?  i do not want to take it to get it vacuum tested and have them run that smoke through it to find if it has a leak.  I don't have the money for that right now.  Thanks people  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR><A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>Preferred Performance</A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||GT Bastard||01-27-2001||08:21 PM||||It sounds like a bad cat converter to me... I've seen it many times before.  Either that or you're running wayyy lean.||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||01-27-2001||08:53 PM||||Yup, GT's right..either clogged cat, way lean, major vacuum leak, timing way off.||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||01-27-2001||09:12 PM||||The EGR valve reduces the combustion temperature by introducing or re-circulating exhaust gas back into the intake manifold, which is an inert gas. The reason for this is to lower NOx emissions, which is caused by high combustion temperatures. It also helps prevent detonation. Detonation can ruin an engine in a very short period of time. <P>Disconnecting the EGR valve does not give your car more power. Disconnecting the EGR valve on an engine that that does not have a mass air flow sensor like the fiero can result in lean air fuel mixtures. A vacuum leak can cause your fuel mixture to go lean causing the glowing manifolds and a clogged catalytic converter will cause your manifolds to glow red also. Your converter will glow red too. If there is a hole in the diaphragm of the EGR valve than yes you could have a vacuum leak through the EGR valve even though you disconnected the vacuum line.<P>Your going to crack your manifolds if you continue to drive your car like this and maybe even burn an exhaust valve of melt a piston. <P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Black88GT||01-27-2001||09:34 PM||||If I'm not mistaked, Shaun has the chip that eliminates the EGR valve, right?<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000005||bHooper||01-27-2001||10:35 PM||||check all your vacuum lines!<P>i had this happen when i first put my GT back together, last spring.<P>you may want to do a search under "glowing manifolds"<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FST2M6||01-28-2001||11:14 AM||||i'd put $ on the cat... he's running nitrous.. and that what killed my cat.(86SE) the cat being toosmall and clagged made the GT slow and the manifolds glow... i got a 2.5" unit from Catco and POOF no more nightlites!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Got2manyfieros||01-28-2001||12:37 PM||||You need to get your EGR tube and valve up to snuff, and your car will be fine.  In otherwords, 88formula is right.||||reg||1
Z||000008||G-Nasty||01-28-2001||11:29 PM||||My factory exhaust manifolds lit up like christmas tree lights also. This happened after a HI-PO rebuild using crane compucam roller rockers crane springs polished racing valves and polished and ported heads. It turn out to be the valves were adjusted incorrectly. They glowed orange and I had poor performance...the combustion explosion was "leaking" into the exhaust. Good Luck-||||reg||1
Z||000009||Shaun41178||01-29-2001||04:43 PM||||thanks guys  I will check to see if my cat glows too.  I don't think it does.  I think it is a vacuum leak cause the idle is a bit high too.  i need to get a timing light on it too just to make sure.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR><A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>Preferred Performance</A>||||reg||1
